# Jena six-hour temperature forecast: test results
Test years 2015, 2016; 17,377 hourly issue times, 99.5% of all hourly issue times in those years. Every model is scored on the same issue times.
| Model | MAE (°C) | RMSE (°C) | Bias (°C) | MAE skill | RMSE skill |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Persistence, T(t+6h) = T(t) | 3.256 | 4.295 | +0.001 | +0.0% | +0.0% |
| Daily persistence, T(t+6h) = T(t-18h) | 2.618 | 3.420 | +0.009 | +19.6% | +20.4% |
| Ridge, calendar recipe | 1.967 | 2.565 | -0.173 | +39.6% | +40.3% |
| Ridge, history recipe | 1.704 | 2.210 | -0.091 | +47.7% | +48.6% |
Skill is `1 - error / persistence error`. Hourly forecast errors are strongly correlated, so these are point estimates, not independent samples.
wrote metrics.json, report.md, week_winter.html, week_summer.html to both/runs/weather
